WEBVTT

00:00:18.256 --> 00:00:19.736
What are you doing?

00:00:19.779 --> 00:00:21.085
Sometimes I hum
warp engine sounds

00:00:21.129 --> 00:00:22.782
just to, you know,
soothe myself.

00:00:22.826 --> 00:00:24.523
Well, that is not what
the engine sounds like.

00:00:24.567 --> 00:00:26.525
Duh. That was Enterprise-D
at warp 4.

00:00:26.569 --> 00:00:28.092
This is Cerritos.

00:00:30.051 --> 00:00:31.487
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
I get it.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:33.750
It's like...

00:00:33.793 --> 00:00:36.579
Fletcher, no. The Cerritoshas
inverted plasma distributors,

00:00:36.622 --> 00:00:38.102
so it's a little bit
higher pitch, like...

00:00:39.756 --> 00:00:42.541
Wrong. The shhzdoesn't come
from the distributors.

00:00:42.585 --> 00:00:44.717
It's the vibrations in thedilithium dispersement manifold.

00:00:44.761 --> 00:00:46.067
It's like this.
Fzzzzz...

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:47.764
No, guys, guys, it's like this. Shhh...

00:00:47.807 --> 00:00:49.766
Dude, I'm telling you,
it's Fzzz...

00:00:49.809 --> 00:00:51.507
And Voyagerwas all...
jzzz...

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:53.378
Are we doing the engine sounds?

00:00:53.422 --> 00:00:54.423
Hchhhh...

00:00:57.034 --> 00:00:58.557
Security to Deck 11.

00:00:58.601 --> 00:01:00.124
Something is very wrong
down here.

00:01:00.168 --> 00:01:01.865
On the ground, now!

00:01:01.908 --> 00:01:03.084
-Ah!
-We're just humming the...
-I said freeze!

00:01:04.563 --> 00:01:07.131
Oh, it is a little higher.

00:02:16.113 --> 00:02:20.900
SHAXS: Security log, stardate 57663.9.

00:02:20.944 --> 00:02:23.947
Our standoff with Drookmani
scavengers continues.

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:27.516
Their claim of salvage on
Starfleet cargo is ludicrous.

00:02:27.559 --> 00:02:30.997
Thus far, my recommendation of
full assault has been ignored

00:02:31.041 --> 00:02:32.173
in favor of a more...

00:02:32.216 --> 00:02:34.218
diplomatic approach.

00:02:34.262 --> 00:02:36.220
As I've already said, Captain,

00:02:36.264 --> 00:02:39.180
while we appreciate your
discovery of this cargo,

00:02:39.223 --> 00:02:41.530
we can only offer you
a finder's reward.

00:02:41.573 --> 00:02:43.967
This trash is ours.
We claim salvage.

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:45.098
It has "Starfleet"
stamped on it.

00:02:45.142 --> 00:02:46.099
That's our trash.

00:02:46.143 --> 00:02:47.579
It's been abandoned

00:02:47.623 --> 00:02:49.102
for more than 100 years!

00:02:49.146 --> 00:02:51.017
That means it's clear
for salvage.

00:02:51.061 --> 00:02:52.541
We're taking it!

00:02:54.543 --> 00:02:56.675
BARNES: Captain, they're
attempting to load that cargo

00:02:56.719 --> 00:02:58.503
-with their tractor beam.
-Oh, no, they didn't.

00:02:58.547 --> 00:02:59.678
Engage our tractor beam.

00:03:05.293 --> 00:03:08.209
Those crates are brimming with
unique Starfleet technology.

00:03:08.252 --> 00:03:09.688
We can't let them have it.

00:03:09.732 --> 00:03:11.821
If we fire on them,
it's an act of war.

00:03:11.864 --> 00:03:13.997
-I advise we fire on them.
-Shaxs!

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:15.259
Shields up.
Yellow alert.

00:03:15.303 --> 00:03:17.261
Our goal is that
this doesn't turn violent.

00:03:17.305 --> 00:03:21.222
But if it does, our crew is
ready and focused.

00:03:21.265 --> 00:03:23.876
ALL :Fletcher! Fletcher! Fletcher...

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:25.791
That's like three cantaloupes
worth of purée.

00:03:25.835 --> 00:03:27.880
-He could beat the record!
-He's doing it!

00:03:27.924 --> 00:03:29.273
Come on, Fletcher,
sloupe that 'loupe!

00:03:29.317 --> 00:03:32.233
-Whoo-hoo! Ooh...
-Aah!

00:03:32.276 --> 00:03:34.539
Do you know how hard it is
to get cheese out of fur

00:03:34.583 --> 00:03:36.019
in a sonic shower?!

00:03:36.062 --> 00:03:38.239
Oh, no, I am so, so sorry.
I didn't mean to.

00:03:38.282 --> 00:03:40.197
Don't try to butter
my bread, Ensign.

00:03:40.241 --> 00:03:41.720
I've heard about you.

00:03:41.764 --> 00:03:44.114
-But I didn't-- What?
-You're a disgrace.

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:47.117
You want to goof around?
Go work on Starbase 80.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.075
-MALE: Damn. Starbase 80?

00:03:49.119 --> 00:03:51.861
Oh, I'm sorry, I didn't realizecats ate nachos.

00:03:51.904 --> 00:03:53.079
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:03:53.123 --> 00:03:54.559
All right, all right, all right.Here, Doc.

00:03:54.603 --> 00:03:56.082
-Here's a warm towel.
-Give me that!

00:03:56.126 --> 00:03:58.868
And some freshly replicated
nachos.

00:03:58.911 --> 00:04:01.653
Try the carnitas.
It's delicioso.

00:04:01.697 --> 00:04:04.177
At least someone around here
appreciates rank.

00:04:04.221 --> 00:04:06.005
-Mm...
-Don't listen to her.

00:04:06.049 --> 00:04:08.051
-She's just a cat in a coat.

00:04:08.094 --> 00:04:09.095
Thanks for defusing that,
Fletch.

00:04:09.139 --> 00:04:10.706
I was about to go nuts.

00:04:10.749 --> 00:04:12.664
Fletcher's like a natural
peace negotiator.

00:04:12.708 --> 00:04:13.839
He was always getting us
out of trouble

00:04:13.883 --> 00:04:14.884
back in the Academy.

00:04:14.927 --> 00:04:16.755
Ha. Remember when
those Nausicans

00:04:16.799 --> 00:04:18.279
tried to eat your heart?

00:04:18.322 --> 00:04:20.585
Yeah, until you convinced them
just to spit in my face.

00:04:20.629 --> 00:04:21.934
I was lucky you were there.

00:04:21.978 --> 00:04:23.762
Uh, Mariner, you were lucky
he was here, too.

00:04:23.806 --> 00:04:25.242
You know,
it's not very Starfleet

00:04:25.286 --> 00:04:26.722
to take a swing
at the bridge crew.

00:04:26.765 --> 00:04:28.724
Whatever. I'm Starfleet as hell.

00:04:28.767 --> 00:04:30.116
And if somebody brings up
Starbase 80,

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:31.596
they better be ready
to throw down.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:32.989
Hey, Mariner, don't let
the senior officers

00:04:33.032 --> 00:04:34.251
get in your head.

00:04:34.295 --> 00:04:35.948
You wouldn't be here
if you weren't great.

00:04:35.992 --> 00:04:37.602
'Cause there's a baseline
of goodness

00:04:37.646 --> 00:04:39.038
to everyone in Starfleet.

00:04:39.082 --> 00:04:40.649
Even Boimler.

00:04:42.781 --> 00:04:46.307
So, um, what do you think's
in that cargo

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:47.873
that has everyone so wound up?

00:04:47.917 --> 00:04:49.266
A bunch of cryo-frozen
princesses

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:50.615
or maybe some fruit?

00:04:50.659 --> 00:04:52.182
Ooh, I hope it's
old communicators.

00:04:52.225 --> 00:04:53.618
You know, the original
clamshell design.

00:04:53.662 --> 00:04:55.141
Ah! Do you think
we're going to find out?

00:04:55.185 --> 00:04:56.969
Once they figure things out
with those aliens,

00:04:57.013 --> 00:04:59.015
they'll probably us space walk
to get everything cataloged.

00:04:59.058 --> 00:05:00.669
Uh, space walk? Really?

00:05:00.712 --> 00:05:02.627
W-Why can't we just use
the cargo transporter?

00:05:02.671 --> 00:05:04.281
-That stuff's too massive.
-Ah...

00:05:04.325 --> 00:05:06.327
Wait, what's wrong? I thought
you loved archival cataloging.

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:07.850
You talk about it
all the time.

00:05:07.893 --> 00:05:09.852
I have a horrible secret.

00:05:09.895 --> 00:05:12.115
I never finished my space-walk
unit at the Academy.

00:05:12.158 --> 00:05:13.377
What? How did you graduate?

00:05:13.421 --> 00:05:14.770
I don't know.
He just gave me a "B,"

00:05:14.813 --> 00:05:16.032
and I didn't say anything.

00:05:16.075 --> 00:05:17.294
It must have been
a clerical error.

00:05:17.338 --> 00:05:19.383
I'm a monster.
Why didn't I just confess?!

00:05:19.427 --> 00:05:21.167
Spacewalking is easy.

00:05:21.211 --> 00:05:23.996
You just float and magnet.
Float and magnet.

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:25.694
But what if I forget to magnet?!

00:05:25.737 --> 00:05:27.086
I'll spin out into
the void of space

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:29.132
and burn up in the atmosphere
of a gas giant.

00:05:29.175 --> 00:05:30.176
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.
Calm down.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:31.526
That's not gonna happen.

00:05:31.569 --> 00:05:33.179
Listen, I've been working on
this new holodeck

00:05:33.223 --> 00:05:34.180
training program.

00:05:34.224 --> 00:05:35.399
I think it can help you.

00:05:35.443 --> 00:05:37.053
-You want to try it out?
-Oh, my gosh, yes.

00:05:37.096 --> 00:05:39.316
Thank you. Thank you
so much, Rutherford. Ah!

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:41.884
The holodeck. Gah, why didn't Ithink of that sooner?

00:05:41.927 --> 00:05:43.886
Yeah, you know, it's not justfor hanging with Sherlock Holmes

00:05:43.929 --> 00:05:46.192
and Robin Hood and Sigmund Freud
and Cyrano de Bergerac

00:05:46.236 --> 00:05:47.803
and Einstein and da Vinci
and Stephen Hawking

00:05:47.846 --> 00:05:48.978
and Socrates...

00:05:49.021 --> 00:05:52.851
Oh, five isolinear
cores down and,

00:05:52.895 --> 00:05:54.418
ugh, just a ton more to go.

00:05:54.462 --> 00:05:57.247
You know, when you call
something a "core,"

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:58.944
it implies there's going to be
one big one,

00:05:58.988 --> 00:06:00.424
not a million little ones.

00:06:00.468 --> 00:06:02.426
Ugh, we're not gonna make it
to the Chu Chu dance.

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:04.428
I traded Kowalski 12 shifts
so I could go.

00:06:04.472 --> 00:06:06.038
Chu Chu dance?

00:06:06.082 --> 00:06:08.084
That sounds awesome.
Is it really that good?

00:06:08.127 --> 00:06:09.825
Oh, yeah.I saw the Zebulon Sisters do it

00:06:09.868 --> 00:06:11.392
back on Deep Space 3,
and I am just now

00:06:11.435 --> 00:06:13.045
coming down from the high.

00:06:13.089 --> 00:06:14.482
-Chu Chu!
-Chu Chu.

00:06:14.525 --> 00:06:17.398
-Oh, great.
Everybody's going except us.
-Guys.

00:06:17.441 --> 00:06:18.877
I can handle this on my own.

00:06:18.921 --> 00:06:20.226
Go get your Chu Chu on.

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:22.228
Oh, no, no, no, we would not
make you do that.

00:06:22.272 --> 00:06:24.405
You would do the same for me.
I've got this.

00:06:24.448 --> 00:06:26.145
Lower Deckers stick together.

00:06:26.189 --> 00:06:28.191
Fletcher,
that is super cool, man.

00:06:28.234 --> 00:06:30.019
Hell yeah. Thanks, Fletcher.

00:06:30.062 --> 00:06:31.063
Mariner, let's go get
our Chu Chu shirts.

00:06:31.107 --> 00:06:32.282
We have Chu Chu shirts?

00:06:32.325 --> 00:06:33.762
Yeah, I made us Chu Chu shirts,come on.

00:06:33.805 --> 00:06:34.937
BOTH:
Chu Chu!

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:37.940
Ah, back to work.

00:06:37.983 --> 00:06:40.725
RUTHERFORD:
All right, don't you worry.

00:06:40.769 --> 00:06:42.466
My program will
have you spacewalking

00:06:42.510 --> 00:06:43.772
with the best of 'em.

00:06:43.815 --> 00:06:47.340
Computer, load Rutherford
Training Beta 2.5.

00:06:48.907 --> 00:06:49.952
Aah!

00:06:49.995 --> 00:06:51.736
Hi. Can I teach you a lesson?

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:53.390
Aw. Well, who's this little guy?

00:06:53.434 --> 00:06:54.739
This is Badgey.

00:06:54.783 --> 00:06:56.480
He's a virtual tutor
who can walk you through

00:06:56.524 --> 00:06:59.091
any Starfleet exercise
you can imagine.

00:06:59.135 --> 00:07:00.484
Aw, look at his little arms.

00:07:00.528 --> 00:07:01.920
Yeah, I made him cute.

00:07:01.964 --> 00:07:04.227
Hi, Badgey, I'm Tendi.

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:06.272
Hi. Can I teach you a lesson?

00:07:06.316 --> 00:07:07.839
Yes, um, can you show me
how to perform

00:07:07.883 --> 00:07:09.754
an untethered cargo retrieval
in open space?

00:07:12.148 --> 00:07:14.455
Sometimes it takes a second.

00:07:14.498 --> 00:07:16.500
You got it.

00:07:18.241 --> 00:07:20.765
Wow, you coded this yourself?

00:07:20.809 --> 00:07:22.158
Yeah, it's just a hobby.

00:07:22.201 --> 00:07:24.116
-But the gravitational waves
were tricky.
-Ah!

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:26.205
Oh, uh, uh...

00:07:26.249 --> 00:07:27.511
So this is spacewalking?

00:07:27.555 --> 00:07:28.773
I like it.

00:07:28.817 --> 00:07:29.948
Just don't get your magnet bootstoo close to...

00:07:29.992 --> 00:07:31.167
Oh!

00:07:32.995 --> 00:07:34.779
Oh, we're stuck together.

00:07:34.823 --> 00:07:36.215
I think we're stuck together.

00:07:36.259 --> 00:07:39.349
Oh, sorry. Yeah.
Let me just...

00:07:39.392 --> 00:07:41.960
Looks like you want
to recover lost cargo.

00:07:42.004 --> 00:07:44.136
-Did I get that right?
-Oh, yeah. Almost forgot.

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:45.311
Coming right up.

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:50.360
Wow, look at him--
Look at him try.

00:07:50.403 --> 00:07:51.970
Ugh, that shouldn't happen.

00:07:52.014 --> 00:07:54.886
Badgey, restart cargo recovery.

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:57.106
Badgey, restart sequence!

00:07:57.149 --> 00:07:58.150
Sorry, it usually works.

00:07:58.194 --> 00:07:59.282
Badgey, stop it!

00:07:59.325 --> 00:08:00.544
Uh, no, it's-it's nothing,
really.

00:08:00.588 --> 00:08:02.154
Come on, you stupid glitch.

00:08:03.112 --> 00:08:06.463
We're back in business.

00:08:10.032 --> 00:08:12.513
I can't believe
I actually made eye contact

00:08:12.556 --> 00:08:14.515
with one of the Zebulon Sisters.

00:08:14.558 --> 00:08:16.342
Oh, God, I forgot
how to breathe.

00:08:16.386 --> 00:08:18.867
Oh, my God, and then,
when they added the third Chu,

00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:21.173
and they were doing
the Chu Chu Chu dance?

00:08:21.217 --> 00:08:22.566
They're geniuses.

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:25.177
I'm glad we
did this together, Boims.

00:08:25.221 --> 00:08:27.440
Sometimes you can be, like,
really not annoying.

00:08:27.484 --> 00:08:29.573
Yeah. Sometimes you can be
not annoying, too.

00:08:30.618 --> 00:08:31.836
Fletcher!

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:34.839
-Oh, no, I'm so woozy.
-Are you okay?

00:08:34.883 --> 00:08:36.362
-What happened?
-Oh...

00:08:36.406 --> 00:08:39.583
The core.
I was working on the core.

00:08:39.627 --> 00:08:43.369
Everything was going fine,
until...

00:08:46.068 --> 00:08:48.549
I couldn't move.
I-I couldn't breathe.

00:08:48.592 --> 00:08:50.202
Fletcher, you tell me
who did this to you.

00:08:50.246 --> 00:08:51.595
Uh, I don't know.

00:08:51.639 --> 00:08:53.379
Next thing I knew,
you were here,

00:08:53.423 --> 00:08:55.120
and now I'm saying this.

00:08:55.164 --> 00:08:56.992
Guys, somebody made off with
one of the isolinear cores

00:08:57.035 --> 00:08:58.036
for the shield array

00:08:58.080 --> 00:08:59.603
Is that important?

00:08:59.647 --> 00:09:02.258
Kinda. They regulate auto-repairwhen the shield's damaged.

00:09:02.301 --> 00:09:03.694
I messed up the shields?

00:09:03.738 --> 00:09:05.870
Hey, hey, it's okay.It's like a backup of a backup.

00:09:05.914 --> 00:09:07.045
Seems like somebody wanted
to get you in trouble

00:09:07.089 --> 00:09:08.438
without damaging the ship.

00:09:08.481 --> 00:09:10.048
The next time the bridge
runs a shield diagnostic,

00:09:10.092 --> 00:09:11.397
they'll definitely notice
it's missing.

00:09:11.441 --> 00:09:13.878
I'm gonna get court-martialed.

00:09:13.922 --> 00:09:15.227
No, you're not.
We can figure this out

00:09:15.271 --> 00:09:16.402
before anyone notices.

00:09:16.446 --> 00:09:17.708
We're the ones who
left you alone.

00:09:17.752 --> 00:09:19.492
We have to work together
to get that core back.

00:09:19.536 --> 00:09:21.364
Okay, who's shady as hell

00:09:21.407 --> 00:09:23.148
and knows this system
as well as we do?

00:09:23.192 --> 00:09:25.934
ALL:
Delta Shift.

00:09:25.977 --> 00:09:28.066
These creepy Delta Shift guys
have always

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:29.633
rubbed me the wrong way.

00:09:29.677 --> 00:09:32.114
I mean, what, they do our jobs
while we sleep? So weird.

00:09:32.157 --> 00:09:33.115
KARAVITUS:
Check it out, guys.

00:09:33.158 --> 00:09:34.420
Beta Shifters.

00:09:34.464 --> 00:09:36.553
Shouldn't you guys be
getting ready for bed?

00:09:36.597 --> 00:09:39.077
Hey, which one of you jerks

00:09:39.121 --> 00:09:41.253
never bothers to wipe down
the diagnostic panel?

00:09:41.297 --> 00:09:42.559
Other people use that thing.

00:09:42.603 --> 00:09:44.300
-Um...-Look, we don't want to be here.

00:09:44.343 --> 00:09:46.215
I don't like us being awake
at the same time.

00:09:46.258 --> 00:09:48.347
It feels wrong, okay?
But we need some answers.

00:09:48.391 --> 00:09:51.481
Oh, damn, this must be
the Beta Shift's version

00:09:51.524 --> 00:09:52.525
of a badass.

00:09:52.569 --> 00:09:54.179
Mariner's a total badass!

00:09:54.223 --> 00:09:55.659
And if you don't come clean,
she's gonna

00:09:55.703 --> 00:09:57.139
your  off!

00:09:57.182 --> 00:09:59.358
Whoa, Fletcher, ease up, man.

00:09:59.402 --> 00:10:00.621
Guys, I'm not gonna do that.
I'm so sorry.

00:10:00.664 --> 00:10:02.318
Just give us the core,
we'll go,

00:10:02.361 --> 00:10:04.363
-and this can all be over.
-What core?

00:10:04.407 --> 00:10:07.105
Oh, please. Puh-lease!

00:10:07.149 --> 00:10:09.194
Look, someone knocked
Fletcher out

00:10:09.238 --> 00:10:10.674
and stole an isolinear core.

00:10:10.718 --> 00:10:12.502
Are you accusing us of assault?

00:10:12.545 --> 00:10:13.634
Get out of here!

00:10:13.677 --> 00:10:15.157
We don't know anything
about a core.

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:16.941
That's it.
You want some of this?

00:10:16.985 --> 00:10:18.551
Where's the core?
Where's the core?

00:10:18.595 --> 00:10:19.857
-Where's the core, dude?
Where's the core?
-Guys, no, no.

00:10:19.901 --> 00:10:20.684
-Don't undo your flaps.
-Do you want to dance?

00:10:20.728 --> 00:10:22.251
I'll take you to the dance.

00:10:22.294 --> 00:10:24.209
I'll pick you up
at your mom and dad's house.

00:10:24.253 --> 00:10:25.515
You don't talk about my dad!

00:10:25.558 --> 00:10:27.299
Wait, hold on.
When did this all go down?

00:10:27.343 --> 00:10:29.127
Uh, I don't know.
A few hours ago.

00:10:29.171 --> 00:10:31.695
What? We were at
the Chu Chu dance with you.

00:10:31.739 --> 00:10:34.002
Oh, yeah.

00:10:34.045 --> 00:10:35.656
-Oh!
-Chu Chu-- Chu Chu dance.

00:10:35.699 --> 00:10:36.961
Wow. A double dance.
Chu Chu dance.

00:10:37.005 --> 00:10:38.571
Oh, my God, Chu Chu dance.

00:10:38.615 --> 00:10:40.661
And at the end,
when they added the third Chu

00:10:40.704 --> 00:10:42.314
and it became
the Chu Chu Chu dance,

00:10:42.358 --> 00:10:44.534
I cried. I saw you crying, too.Don't even lie.

00:10:44.577 --> 00:10:46.231
Oh, damn, you werethere.

00:10:46.275 --> 00:10:48.669
Yeah, that checks out.It had to be someone else, man.

00:10:48.712 --> 00:10:49.974
Don't you remember anything?

00:10:50.018 --> 00:10:51.541
I don't know. It was dark.

00:10:51.584 --> 00:10:53.412
It was totally dark.
Couldn't see anything.

00:10:53.456 --> 00:10:54.413
-ALL: Whoa!

00:10:54.457 --> 00:10:56.502
Did they just fire on us?

00:10:56.546 --> 00:10:58.504
Impossible. These guys
don't even have weapons.

00:10:58.548 --> 00:11:00.332
The Drookmani have reversed
their tractor beam

00:11:00.376 --> 00:11:03.031
to launch the cargo
against our hull.

00:11:04.423 --> 00:11:07.470
These guys are luckyI'm so ethical and considerate.

00:11:17.045 --> 00:11:18.742
Captain, something is wrong
with our shields.

00:11:18.786 --> 00:11:20.178
They shouldn't be fading
this fast.

00:11:20.222 --> 00:11:21.571
Permission to destroy
the enemy ship.

00:11:21.614 --> 00:11:23.268
They're trying to bait us
into a fight.

00:11:23.312 --> 00:11:25.575
We have to find a way
to end this peacefully.

00:11:25.618 --> 00:11:27.403
We're Starfleet, damn it.

00:11:33.148 --> 00:11:34.410
-Whoa!
-What? Aah!

00:11:34.453 --> 00:11:36.194
COMPUTER:
Non-essential power diverted.

00:11:36.238 --> 00:11:37.718
Safety protocols disabled.

00:11:37.761 --> 00:11:39.154
What the heck?

00:11:39.197 --> 00:11:40.721
Uh, we should get out of here.
Computer, end program.

00:11:40.764 --> 00:11:43.506
-I said computer, end program.

00:11:43.549 --> 00:11:44.725
-That's not good.

00:11:44.768 --> 00:11:46.030
Badgey, run diagnostic.

00:11:46.074 --> 00:11:47.553
You got it.

00:11:47.597 --> 00:11:48.554
Ow!

00:11:48.598 --> 00:11:50.382
Sorry about that.

00:11:50.426 --> 00:11:54.212
I didn't mean to hurt you.

00:11:54.256 --> 00:11:55.692
Badgey, what the hell?

00:11:55.736 --> 00:11:58.782
Oh, guess I'm just
a stupid, worthless glitch!

00:11:58.826 --> 00:12:00.044
Oh. Badgey?

00:12:00.088 --> 00:12:01.567
Computer, re-engage
safety protocols.

00:12:01.611 --> 00:12:03.178
COMPUTER:
Safety protocols are
unavailable.

00:12:06.834 --> 00:12:08.270
Get off me.
He's corrupted!

00:12:09.706 --> 00:12:12.665
Can I teach you a lesson?

00:12:17.801 --> 00:12:20.673
Computer,
load Bajoran marketplace!

00:12:22.632 --> 00:12:24.460
Put this on, put this on.
We got to blend in.

00:12:29.857 --> 00:12:31.772
We got to keep going.

00:12:31.815 --> 00:12:33.077
-Fun fact,

00:12:33.121 --> 00:12:35.123
I'm gonna rip your eyes out!

00:12:35.166 --> 00:12:36.733
That fact wasn't fun!

00:12:50.529 --> 00:12:52.967
Our shields can't take
much more of this.

00:12:53.010 --> 00:12:54.185
These guys are begging
for a fight.

00:12:54.229 --> 00:12:55.796
I say we give it to 'em.

00:12:55.839 --> 00:12:57.449
Phasers locked
onto their warp core, Captain.

00:12:57.493 --> 00:12:59.756
Please, please let me
shoot their warp core.

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:01.105
I have been very good
this month.

00:13:01.149 --> 00:13:04.239
-Evasive pattern Sulu-Alpha.
-Oh, come on!

00:13:04.282 --> 00:13:08.025
I thought you said this trash
wasn't worth fighting for.

00:13:08.069 --> 00:13:09.200
We're not fighting.

00:13:09.244 --> 00:13:11.028
Avoiding damage is fighting.

00:13:11.072 --> 00:13:13.248
We can talk this out.

00:13:13.291 --> 00:13:14.466
you.

00:13:19.515 --> 00:13:21.822
Oh, man, the shields
must be slammed.

00:13:21.865 --> 00:13:24.259
If they fall below 50%,they'll realize the core's gone.

00:13:24.302 --> 00:13:25.826
-And then I'll be gone.
-Wait, wait, wait.

00:13:25.869 --> 00:13:27.088
I thought Drookmani
were just scavengers.

00:13:27.131 --> 00:13:29.394
The Drookmani!
I bet they took the core,

00:13:29.438 --> 00:13:31.048
to mess with our defenses.

00:13:31.092 --> 00:13:32.528
The guy who zapped me
was definitely an alien.

00:13:32.571 --> 00:13:34.008
We got to report this
to the bridge.

00:13:34.051 --> 00:13:36.010
Whoa, hold up. We got to scan
the ship for intruders,

00:13:36.053 --> 00:13:37.446
I'm not going to the captain
without proof.

00:13:37.489 --> 00:13:40.275
Okay, let's go.
Let's go get our scanners.

00:13:40.318 --> 00:13:41.798
Okay, listen.

00:13:41.842 --> 00:13:43.104
I'll search decks
two through ten.

00:13:43.147 --> 00:13:45.193
Fletcher, you-- the... Huh?

00:13:45.236 --> 00:13:48.326
The core?
Fletcher, it was in your bunk?

00:13:48.370 --> 00:13:51.068
Uh, uh, aliens.
It's, uh, aliens.

00:13:51.112 --> 00:13:53.375
Those frickin' aliens,
I knew they'd do this.

00:13:53.418 --> 00:13:54.811
They're gonna frame me.

00:13:54.855 --> 00:13:56.291
-I knew it.
-Fletcher.

00:13:56.334 --> 00:13:59.381
I messed up, you guys.

00:13:59.424 --> 00:14:01.165
Oh, man, I really messed up.

00:14:01.209 --> 00:14:02.906
-I'm the worst! I'm slime!
-Stop it!

00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:05.169
-Get ahold of yourself
and shut up.
-Stupid, stupid Fletcher!

00:14:05.213 --> 00:14:07.258
Just tell us what you did.

00:14:07.302 --> 00:14:09.391
When you guys went
to the Chu Chu dance,

00:14:09.434 --> 00:14:12.176
I was doing all that
rewiring on my own,

00:14:12.220 --> 00:14:15.484
and it was getting so hard,
so, I was like,

00:14:15.527 --> 00:14:18.313
"This would be so much easier
if I were smarter."

00:14:18.356 --> 00:14:20.881
And then I was like,
"Wait. The computer's smart.

00:14:20.924 --> 00:14:23.361
-Maybe it can make me smart."
-What?

00:14:23.405 --> 00:14:25.363
FLETCHER:
So I hooked it up
directly to my brain,

00:14:25.407 --> 00:14:27.278
and let it run
so it would make me smarter.

00:14:27.322 --> 00:14:29.454
MARINER:
Ooh, boy,
that is not a good idea.

00:14:29.498 --> 00:14:31.543
COMPUTER:
Neural pathway established.

00:14:36.026 --> 00:14:37.332
FLETCHER:
But I didn't get smarter.

00:14:37.375 --> 00:14:39.334
It broke and I peed my pants.

00:14:39.377 --> 00:14:41.031
So I hid down here
and told you guys

00:14:41.075 --> 00:14:42.990
I had been attacked
so you wouldn't feel let down.

00:14:43.033 --> 00:14:45.166
Yeah, I don't kn-- uh, I don't
know what to do with this.

00:14:45.209 --> 00:14:47.385
We're supposed to have each
other's backs, Fletcher!

00:14:47.429 --> 00:14:49.910
You were gonna lie to the
captain about an alien attack?

00:14:49.953 --> 00:14:51.172
You could have started a war.

00:14:51.215 --> 00:14:52.869
Come on, just back me up.

00:14:52.913 --> 00:14:55.089
All we do is back you up,
and all you do is lie!

00:14:55.132 --> 00:14:57.482
I just wanted you
to be proud of me.

00:14:57.526 --> 00:14:59.876
-I messed up.

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:01.878
It's-- ugh-- it's okay.

00:15:01.922 --> 00:15:04.098
We can reformat the core
and put this all behind us.

00:15:04.141 --> 00:15:06.100
-I guess.
-Really?

00:15:06.143 --> 00:15:08.276
Oh, thanks, you guys.

00:15:08.319 --> 00:15:10.278
You know, I've actually
learned a lot today.

00:15:10.321 --> 00:15:12.410
This has been, like,
a learning experience for me.

00:15:12.454 --> 00:15:14.282
That's all that matters.
And you know what?

00:15:14.325 --> 00:15:17.328
We're Starfleet.
We are Starfleet.

00:15:17.372 --> 00:15:20.288
-And when we make
mistakes, we learn...

00:15:28.731 --> 00:15:29.993
Fix it! Fix it! Fix it! Fix it!

00:15:30.037 --> 00:15:32.256
-What did you do to it?
-I don't know!

00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:34.693
CORE :
Make me smarter.
Make me smarter.

00:15:34.737 --> 00:15:36.347
Ugh, Fletcher, your brain wavescorrupted that thing.

00:15:36.391 --> 00:15:39.220
It's incorporating anything
it can get its grabber on.

00:15:39.263 --> 00:15:42.005
-Fletcher, you've got
to call this in!
-But I'll get in trouble!

00:15:42.049 --> 00:15:44.703
-If this thing gets loose
it could mess up the ship.
-CORE: Show me something!

00:15:44.747 --> 00:15:46.183
Alert the captain right now!

00:15:46.227 --> 00:15:48.925
You're right. Just let me
get my tricorder here--

00:15:48.969 --> 00:15:52.102
Hello! Die! Die! Die!

00:15:52.146 --> 00:15:54.713
-Fletcher!
-CORE: Dummy!

00:15:54.757 --> 00:15:57.803
Dummy! Party of dumbass!

00:15:57.847 --> 00:16:00.415
-Me smart.
-Get off of me! Let go!

00:16:00.458 --> 00:16:03.853
You help me or I'll say
this was all your idea.

00:16:03.896 --> 00:16:05.202
I'm not going down for this.

00:16:05.246 --> 00:16:08.031
Dude, what you're doing
is so not Starfleet.

00:16:08.075 --> 00:16:09.337
You break rules all the time.

00:16:09.380 --> 00:16:10.947
Only dumb rules
that shouldn't be there

00:16:10.991 --> 00:16:12.296
so I can do a better job.

00:16:12.340 --> 00:16:13.906
I would never
put anyone in danger.

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:16.213
--Except sometimes maybe Boimler.

00:16:16.257 --> 00:16:18.911
-Stupid, stupid Fletcher!

00:16:25.092 --> 00:16:26.484
I'm sorry. This is all my fault.

00:16:26.528 --> 00:16:28.051
Here's a tip.

00:16:28.095 --> 00:16:33.361
I'm going to burn
your hearts in a fire!

00:16:33.404 --> 00:16:35.754
-Leave us alone, Badgey!
-No!

00:16:35.798 --> 00:16:39.062
-You were only trying to help.
-No, I was trying to show off.

00:16:39.106 --> 00:16:41.282
I knew Badgey wasn't ready yet,but I wanted to impress you.

00:16:41.325 --> 00:16:44.111
I just think you're really cool.I'm an idiot.

00:16:44.154 --> 00:16:46.852
Aw, Rutherford,
you impress me every day.

00:16:46.896 --> 00:16:48.332
You're very scientific.

00:16:48.376 --> 00:16:50.334
I mean, Badgey'san amazing piece of programming,

00:16:50.378 --> 00:16:53.120
-even if he does
want to kill us.
-Yeah.

00:16:53.163 --> 00:16:55.035
he is a killing machine,
isn't he?

00:16:55.078 --> 00:16:57.472
It's actually weirdthat he hasn't murdered us yet.

00:16:57.515 --> 00:16:59.343
Hope you're ready to die.

00:16:59.387 --> 00:17:04.000
Just as soon as I...
get up there...

00:17:04.044 --> 00:17:06.263
gonna kill you.

00:17:06.307 --> 00:17:07.830
Aw. Poor little guy's
really having trouble

00:17:07.873 --> 00:17:09.223
with those stairs.

00:17:09.266 --> 00:17:11.790
You've got this, Badgey!
Wait, what am I doing?

00:17:11.834 --> 00:17:13.053
He shouldn't be affected
by the physical parameters

00:17:13.096 --> 00:17:14.315
of the simulation.

00:17:14.358 --> 00:17:17.013
I'm gonna wear your skin!

00:17:17.057 --> 00:17:18.493
Wait, if we're tiring him out,

00:17:18.536 --> 00:17:20.364
then maybe we can
freeze him out.

00:17:20.408 --> 00:17:23.933
Computer, load environment 83.

00:17:25.326 --> 00:17:27.850
Quick. Come on.

00:17:29.025 --> 00:17:30.461
Shield integrity 40%
and dropping.

00:17:30.505 --> 00:17:33.290
Automatic repair is down,
switching to manual.

00:17:33.334 --> 00:17:35.336
CORE:
Dummy! Dummy!

00:17:37.033 --> 00:17:38.469
Quick. Grab that edge,
we got to drag it...

00:17:38.513 --> 00:17:40.341
Guys, wait. I know what to do.

00:17:40.384 --> 00:17:41.820
You figured out how to fix it?

00:17:41.864 --> 00:17:42.995
I wish. No.

00:17:43.039 --> 00:17:44.823
We let this thing
beat us up a little,

00:17:44.867 --> 00:17:46.216
then later we say
that a Q showed up

00:17:46.260 --> 00:17:47.957
and caused all of this.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:50.090
Nobody will doubt us
'cause we'll be all busted up

00:17:50.133 --> 00:17:51.917
and, you know,
Qs are super unpredictable.

00:17:51.961 --> 00:17:53.223
Here, help me feed some stuff

00:17:53.267 --> 00:17:54.398
into this thing
so it gets bigger.

00:17:54.442 --> 00:17:56.313
CORE:
Delicioso.

00:17:56.357 --> 00:17:59.403
Oh, real nice, guys.
Let me out of here! Come on!

00:17:59.447 --> 00:18:01.405
-The Q thing's a good idea!
-CORE: Let go!

00:18:03.146 --> 00:18:05.148
Uh, it just incorporated
a light panel.

00:18:05.192 --> 00:18:06.323
We've got to get it
to the transporter

00:18:06.367 --> 00:18:07.846
before it's too big to move.

00:18:07.890 --> 00:18:09.326
I know you guys were friends
at the Academy,

00:18:09.370 --> 00:18:11.546
but I am just gonna say it:
I do not like Fletcher.

00:18:11.589 --> 00:18:13.548
-Ow! We got to rethink
this whole

00:18:13.591 --> 00:18:15.245
"Lower Decks stands together"
thing.

00:18:15.289 --> 00:18:17.204
-CORE: What you got?
-You know, it's kind of nice

00:18:17.247 --> 00:18:18.857
that wearen't
fighting for once.

00:18:18.901 --> 00:18:20.207
Yeah. I guess we make
a good team.

00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:21.512
-CORE: What you got?
-From now on,

00:18:21.556 --> 00:18:23.123
someLower Deckers
stand together.

00:18:23.166 --> 00:18:24.167
CORE:
Come on, bro, square up.

00:18:24.211 --> 00:18:26.169
Whoa! Oh, no.

00:18:28.389 --> 00:18:29.564
Oh, , there's no way

00:18:29.607 --> 00:18:31.348
we're gonna make it
to the transporter.

00:18:31.392 --> 00:18:32.480
Airlock.

00:18:32.523 --> 00:18:34.177
Aliens. It's, uh, aliens.

00:18:34.221 --> 00:18:35.352
Those frickin aliens!

00:18:35.396 --> 00:18:37.049
Here. Fetch!

00:18:37.093 --> 00:18:39.182
CORE:
Whoa! I got this.

00:18:40.923 --> 00:18:43.186
You don't talk about my dad!

00:18:43.230 --> 00:18:44.883
BOIMLER:
Whew.

00:18:44.927 --> 00:18:48.278
-Oh, that was close.
-Ooh, yeah. Disaster averted.

00:18:48.322 --> 00:18:51.629
MARINER:
Wait, wait. Is it drifting
towards the Drookmani?

00:18:51.673 --> 00:18:54.110
BOTH:
No, no, no, no...

00:18:55.677 --> 00:18:57.635
BOIMLER:
Oh, no.

00:18:57.679 --> 00:18:59.985
We are so getting fired
for this.

00:19:02.684 --> 00:19:04.468
Shields are down, Captain.

00:19:04.512 --> 00:19:08.255
I have done everything I can torespect their sanctity of life,

00:19:08.298 --> 00:19:11.388
to avoid conflict, and give themthe benefit of the doubt.

00:19:11.432 --> 00:19:13.912
The Drookmani
have given me no choice.

00:19:13.956 --> 00:19:15.566
Shaxs, target their warp core.

00:19:15.610 --> 00:19:18.047
Yes!

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:20.223
No! We waited too long.

00:19:20.267 --> 00:19:22.182
Weapons systems are down.

00:19:22.225 --> 00:19:24.358
We need to get the crew
into escape pods now.

00:19:24.401 --> 00:19:25.663
Prepare to abandon ship.

00:19:25.707 --> 00:19:27.361
Wait, Captain. Look.
What is that?

00:19:34.629 --> 00:19:37.588
-Uh...
-We did it!

00:19:37.632 --> 00:19:40.417
I don't know what we did,
but we did it!

00:19:42.245 --> 00:19:45.117
Stay awake, Tendi.
We can do this.

00:19:45.161 --> 00:19:47.598
Did... did we lose him?

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:52.690
Uh, yeah. We're doing fine.

00:19:52.734 --> 00:19:55.258
We're so good. Keep going.

00:19:55.302 --> 00:19:58.174
Ah. Not running anymore, Father?

00:19:58.218 --> 00:19:59.654
This ends now, Badgey.

00:19:59.697 --> 00:20:01.656
After I gut you, I'm gonna slit

00:20:01.699 --> 00:20:03.527
your little green friend's
throat

00:20:03.571 --> 00:20:06.051
and take a bath in her blood.

00:20:06.095 --> 00:20:08.010
No, you're not!

00:20:20.109 --> 00:20:22.503
I'm gonna wear your skin!

00:20:37.431 --> 00:20:39.650
You can't hurt me, Father.

00:20:42.044 --> 00:20:47.179
Maybe with your disappointment,but not with your fists.

00:20:47.223 --> 00:20:49.312
I'm sorry I yelled at you, son.

00:20:49.356 --> 00:20:51.314
I was just trying
to impress Tendi.

00:20:51.358 --> 00:20:53.403
I mean, look at her.
She's so cute.

00:20:53.447 --> 00:20:56.188
It's too late for apologies.

00:20:56.232 --> 00:20:58.626
It's too...

00:20:58.669 --> 00:21:01.063
Kill you...

00:21:01.106 --> 00:21:03.326
So cold. Father?

00:21:05.372 --> 00:21:07.504
I'm so sorry
it came to this, Badgey.

00:21:07.548 --> 00:21:09.027
I'm gonna cut off your foot.

00:21:09.071 --> 00:21:11.508
No. Don't talk.

00:21:11.552 --> 00:21:15.425
-It's over now.
-Diplomatic immunity.

00:21:17.384 --> 00:21:21.344
Badgey!

00:21:23.825 --> 00:21:26.218
Got it. Restoring main power.

00:21:26.262 --> 00:21:29.221
COMPUTER:
Safety protocols restored.

00:21:30.701 --> 00:21:32.355
Hi. Can I teach you a lesson?

00:21:32.399 --> 00:21:34.226
-Oh, hey. Hi, Badgey.
-Um...

00:21:34.270 --> 00:21:37.055
Um, does he remember
he was trying to, uh...

00:21:37.099 --> 00:21:39.275
Remember what?
Can I teach you a lesson?

00:21:39.319 --> 00:21:41.059
Nope, nope, nope, nope.
Actually, you know what?

00:21:41.103 --> 00:21:42.583
-We were just heading out.
-Yeah, yeah, we're-we're good.

00:21:42.626 --> 00:21:44.193
Thanks, Badgey.

00:21:44.236 --> 00:21:47.675
You got it. If you need me,
Badgey's here.

00:21:47.718 --> 00:21:50.068
I'm always here.

00:21:50.112 --> 00:21:52.288
Ow, my frickin' wrists
are all chafed.

00:21:52.332 --> 00:21:53.681
Good. Shut up.

00:21:53.724 --> 00:21:55.683
That core had my brain pattern
all over it.

00:21:55.726 --> 00:21:57.641
If they find it
and kick me off the ship,

00:21:57.685 --> 00:21:59.164
you're going down with me.

00:21:59.208 --> 00:22:00.557
What the hell is going on
down here?

00:22:00.601 --> 00:22:02.472
We've got an unauthorized
airlock ejection,

00:22:02.516 --> 00:22:04.431
a missing computer core,
and somebody attacked

00:22:04.474 --> 00:22:06.128
that Drookmani ship.

00:22:06.171 --> 00:22:08.260
You three better have one hell
of an explanation.

00:22:08.304 --> 00:22:10.785
Oh, I'll tell you
exactly what happened.

00:22:11.873 --> 00:22:13.135
SHAXS:
Ensign Fletcher's

00:22:13.178 --> 00:22:15.137
brilliant improvisation,

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:17.400
updating the isolinear core
to weaponize it

00:22:17.444 --> 00:22:19.533
against the Drookmani
saved the Cerritos.

00:22:19.576 --> 00:22:22.100
Fletcher demonstrated
the sort of selfless heroism

00:22:22.144 --> 00:22:23.754
that Starfleet's all about.

00:22:23.798 --> 00:22:27.105
It's that heroism that
earned him a promotion

00:22:27.149 --> 00:22:30.108
and a transfer to the Titan!

00:22:30.152 --> 00:22:31.414
-FLETCHER: Oh, man.

00:22:31.458 --> 00:22:33.764
Wow.

00:22:33.808 --> 00:22:35.636
Did we have to get him promoted?

00:22:35.679 --> 00:22:37.420
Eh, you know what they say,
keep your friends close

00:22:37.464 --> 00:22:39.596
and your enemies
way the hell somewhere else.

00:22:39.640 --> 00:22:41.163
Whoa. The Titan.

00:22:41.206 --> 00:22:42.512
Isn't that, like,
your dream gig?

00:22:42.556 --> 00:22:44.427
Yeah. It is.

00:22:44.471 --> 00:22:46.386
But you know what, maybe this
is just what Fletcher needs

00:22:46.429 --> 00:22:47.474
to turn things around.

00:22:47.517 --> 00:22:49.389
New ship, new duties.

00:22:49.432 --> 00:22:51.478
It might just make him
a better man.

00:22:53.349 --> 00:22:55.133
I got frickin' fired!

00:22:55.177 --> 00:22:56.526
What? You, fired?

00:22:56.570 --> 00:22:58.746
Who would fire you, ever?

00:22:58.789 --> 00:23:00.661
It's like, who says you're not
supposed to empty trash

00:23:00.704 --> 00:23:02.837
into the warp core?
It all burns up anyway.

00:23:02.880 --> 00:23:05.143
Oh, yeah, who wouldn't make
that mistake?

00:23:05.187 --> 00:23:06.536
I thought maybe you guys
could, like, put in

00:23:06.580 --> 00:23:07.798
-a good word for me or...
-Uh, hey, Fletcher?

00:23:07.842 --> 00:23:09.670
Fletcher. Sorry,
you're breaking up.

00:23:09.713 --> 00:23:11.628
I think you're going through
a temporal rift or something.

00:23:11.672 --> 00:23:14.457
-A rift? What a-- Hello?
-Whoa, Fletcher, there's a Q.

00:23:14.501 --> 00:23:16.546
-I'm holding my badge up...
-There's a Q
doing crazy Q stuff.

00:23:16.590 --> 00:23:18.374
-Got to go.
-Can you hear me? Guys...

00:23:18.418 --> 00:23:20.245
Well, he's Earth's problem now.

00:23:20.289 --> 00:23:22.160
Got to say, I'd rather serve
with a dozen of you

00:23:22.204 --> 00:23:23.466
than one Fletcher.

00:23:23.510 --> 00:23:24.815
I mean, yeah, you break
the rules all the time,

00:23:24.859 --> 00:23:26.513
but at your heart,
you're Starfleet.

00:23:26.556 --> 00:23:28.297
Aw, Boimler. That's really nice.Thanks, man.

00:23:28.340 --> 00:23:29.777
Now come on. I got the keys
to the captain's yacht.

00:23:29.820 --> 00:23:31.213
Wait, what?
You shouldn't have those.

00:23:31.256 --> 00:23:32.693
No, it's cool.I signed them out in your name.

00:23:32.736 --> 00:23:33.781
-Last one there's a Fletcher.
-Wait. No, no, no.

00:23:33.824 --> 00:23:35.043
That's not the lesson here!

00:23:35.086 --> 00:23:36.305
MARINER:
Lower Decks, let's go!
